          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest or lowest hand (or both) at the showdown.',
          gameplay: '1. **Ante**: All players post the ante. 2. **Market Setup**: Dealer turns up two cards and places them beside the deck. 3. **Buy Phase**: Starting left of dealer, each player buys one card from the market (face-up) or stock (top card, revealed on purchase). 4. **Refill**: Purchased market cards are replaced immediately from the stock. 5. **Bet Phase**: After each buy round, a standard betting round. 6. **Repetition**: Buy/bet sequence repeats 5 times until each player has 5 cards. 7. **Declaration**: Active players secret-declare High, Low, or Both using chips in hand. 8. **Showdown**: Cards revealed; pot split per declarations.',
          keyRules: [
            'Market cards cost based on rank: 2-5 (2u), 6-K (1u), Ace (4u).',
            'Cards bought from the stock are revealed to the table immediately.',
            'Market purchases remain face-up if taken from the market row.',
            "Pig Rule: If declaring 'Both', you must win both High and Low halves solo or win nothing.",
            'Each player must buy exactly one card per buy phase (mandatory).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep your 'down' cards a secret while tracking what others buy face-up. Cheap 6-K cards are great for bluffing a high hand.",
          intermediate: 'Aces are versatile but expensive. Only buy them if they complete a flush/straight or a top-tier low.',
          advanced: 'Defensive rank-blocking: If the refill shows a 2 and an opponent is building a low, buy that 2 even if you have a high hand.',
          tips: [
            "Being on the dealer's left is high value; you get the first choice of the fresh market refill.",
            'Check the threshold: Ensure you actually have an 8-low or better before declaring Low.',
            'Track opponent face-up purchases to estimate their declaration direction before chips-in-fist.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
