          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers are used in this game.',
          suitDescription: 'Four suits in the French tradition: spades (piques), hearts (cœurs), diamonds (carreaux), and clubs (trèfles). Each suit contains thirteen cards from ace to two.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks in each suit: ace (high or low by game), king, queen, jack, ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three, and two. Aces play low for the low hand and high for the high hand in this variant.',
