            potPosition: 'center',
          },
        },
        prompts: {
          human: 'Welcome to Abyssinia. Step up to the market where victory is bought, not dealt. You start with an empty hand and a table full of opportunities. Each round, you must buy one card from the face-up market or take a chance on the stock. Watch your budget—high ranks like Aces cost more than commoners. After five rounds of buying and betting, declare your hand: go for High, Low, or both. But beware the Pig Rule—declare Both and fail, and you leave the table empty-handed.',
          ai: 'Game: Abyssinia Poker. Logic: Market-buy phase (5 rounds). Progression: [Ante -> MarketSetup(2 up) -> (BuyPhase -> BetRound) x5 -> SimultaneousDeclare -> Showdown]. Buy costs: Ranks 2-5=2u, 6-K=1u, A=4u, Stock=2u (revealed face-up). Betting: Fixed Limit. Hand eval: High=StandardPoker, Low=AceToFive 8-or-better. Declaration: chips_in_fist {0=Low,1=High,2=Both}. PigRule=true: declaring Both and failing = forfeit pot. Split: 50/50 High/Low; high scoops if no qualifying low. Odd chip to High.',
        },
        scoring: {
          description: 'High-Low Split pot. 50% to the best poker hand, 50% to the best low hand (8-or-better qualifier).',
          winCondition: 'Highest poker rank wins the high half of the pot; lowest qualifying hand (8-high or better) wins the low half.',
          cardValues: {},
          penalties: {
            'The Pig Penalty': "If a player declares 'Both' and fails to win both halves, they forfeit all right to the pot.",
          },
          splitRules: 'The pot is split 50/50 between the best high hand and the best qualifying low hand (8-or-better). If no player qualifies low, the high hand scoops the entire pot. Odd chips go to the high hand winner.',
